PATCH 362: editor ADD-TANK edit-op harness (env-gated FIST_EDIT_ADDTANK, DEFAULT OFF).

The SECOND editor DoD deliverable: drive one EDIT op (ADD TANK) -> save -> verify the delta, on top
of the load->save round-trip (patch 360/361).  Like patch 361 this is an env-gated harness hook in
the ACCEPT cascade FUN_0000_4754, fired right after FUN_0000_d501 has LOADED the selected battle
(AZER1.FSG) into the battle-state DGROUP + the live unit registry, and BEFORE FUN_1000_6015 / the
e4bb game loop.  With FIST_EDIT_ADDTANK set it:
  1. enters EDITING mode faithfully (DAT_2000_2dab |= 2, the bit2=EDITING flag FUN_0000_540a toggles);
  2. adds ONE tank to the battle-state through the engine's REAL unit machinery, then
  3. drives the engine's OWN serializer FUN_0000_d5f9 to save, and exits.

WHY THIS SHAPE (honest scope): the fully-interactive editor add-tank is the map-canvas element's
activate handler FUN_0000_4c7a (dispatched 4aaa->[DGROUP:0x7c54+3c52] tool table, tool-slot 8),
which pops the FUN_0000_64ea vehicle-type picker, projects the click to a world cell via
FUN_0000_3f3c off the map camera-state pointer DAT_1000_d552, and commits the unit.  That path is
gated on the POST-6015 live editor MAP-VIEW (the extender-side 93c0 render, an unreconstructed
frontier -- docs/editor.md sub-deliverable 3): the object-descriptor that 4c7a threads as its unit
record (register DI, param_6) has no statically-resolvable origin before 6015, and 3f3c's cell is
non-deterministic without the map-view camera block initialized.  So the harness does the add
through the SAME roster/registry machinery the proven LOAD path uses -- NOT a fabricated record:
  * FUN_1000_b21d (patch 200) -- the REAL roster allocator: reserves a fresh unit slot in the
    friendly pool (DGROUP:0xa022 stride 0x37) or enemy pool (0xc05c stride 0xfb), keyed on the team
    bit byte[obj-0x19ec]&1, bumps the roster count/high-water/occupancy bitmap, and returns the new
    slot's DGROUP near-offset (its DI return, exposed by patch 200);
  * the new unit's serializable body is cloned from an existing LOADED friendly (tank) unit's record
    -- so it is a genuine, well-formed unit (identical structure to a load-ingested one), guaranteed
    to serialize + reload.  Only the record's serializable prefix (0x37 bytes, exactly what the DCBS
    serializer d6e4 writes and the loader d81e reads back) matters; b21d has already set slot[0]=obj
    and slot[2]=roster-idx, so we clone only the body [+4 .. +0x37);
  * the new slot is registered into the first free entry of the 182-entry unit registry
    DGROUP:0x9fbc (the exact table FUN_0000_c157/c164 -- and hence d84e/d6e4 -- walk on save), with
    the cloned unit's registry value, so the added unit is counted (80 -> 81) and serialized;
  * FUN_1000_66cd(0xd27) posts the real editor status "TANK ADDED" (msgid 0xd27 = STRSEG:0xd27, the
    editor string block image 0x2e467; msgid = image_off - 0x2d740, cf. 540a's 0xcd3 "BATTLE IS
    LOCKED!").
Spatial-index registration (FUN_0000_43c1 -> DGROUP:0x6d3c) is deliberately NOT run here: it is not
needed to SERIALIZE (d6e4 walks 0x9fbc, not 0x6d3c), and the RELOAD (d501->d7e1->d81e->43c1) does it
faithfully on the way back in -- so the save delta stays a clean data mutation.

VERIFICATION (well-formed + deterministic fixed-point, DoD option b -- see docs/editor.md): the
edited save has exactly ONE more DCBS unit than the pre-edit round-trip save (80 -> 81), it RELOADS
via d501 (the added unit is a valid tank), and load(edited)->save is a FIXED POINT
(load->save->load->save byte-identical), native AND wasm, native==wasm 0-diff.  A DOSBox
original-editor byte-compare is not a like-for-like reference (same limitation as patch 361: the
original saves from the post-6015 editing game-loop, a different save-point, and the map-click cell
cannot be pinned identically without the live map-view) -> option (b) with this honest note.

Gated behind getenv (NULL by default) -> the 27 prior verify flows never set it -> BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL.
4754 is only reached on the ACCEPT cascade; the hook precedes the sim so no gameplay state is
perturbed.  b21d/66cd/d5f9 asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -13991,6 +13991,43 @@
     FUN_0000_d5f9(0,0,0,0x79a9,0,0);
     exit(0);
   }
+  if (getenv("FIST_EDIT_ADDTANK")) {
+    /* PATCH 362: editor ADD-TANK edit-op harness (env-gated FIST_EDIT_ADDTANK, DEFAULT OFF ->
+       behaviour-neutral for the verify flows).  After d501 LOADS the battle (80 units in the
+       0x9fbc registry) and BEFORE 6015 / the e4bb loop: enter EDITING mode, add ONE tank through
+       the engine's REAL roster allocator (b21d) + unit registry (0x9fbc), post the "TANK ADDED"
+       status (66cd 0xd27), then drive the serializer d5f9 and exit.  The added unit is cloned
+       from an existing loaded FRIENDLY (tank) unit's serializable record -> a genuine, well-formed
+       unit (80 -> 81), verified by reload + fixed-point.  See this patch's header for the full
+       rationale (the interactive 4c7a map-click UI is blocked on the post-6015 map-view frontier). */
+    extern unsigned char g_fist_cf;
+    unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+    unsigned short *fbc = (unsigned short *)(dg + 0xdfbc);   /* 0x9fbc unit registry {slot,val} x0xb6 */
+    int k, f, i;
+    unsigned short src = 0, val = 0, obj, nrec;
+    DAT_2000_2dab = DAT_2000_2dab | 2;                       /* enter EDITING mode (2dab bit2 = EDIT) */
+    for (k = 0; k < 0xb6; k = k + 1) {                       /* first FRIENDLY loaded unit (team bit 0) */
+      unsigned short s = fbc[k * 2];
+      if (s != 0) {
+        obj = *(unsigned short *)(dg + s);
+        if ((dg[(unsigned short)(obj - 0x19ec)] & 1) == 0) { src = s; val = fbc[k * 2 + 1]; break; }
+      }
+    }
+    if (src != 0) {
+      obj = *(unsigned short *)(dg + src);
+      nrec = (unsigned short)FUN_1000_b21d(obj);            /* REAL roster allocator -> new 0x37 slot */
+      if (!g_fist_cf && nrec != 0) {
+        for (i = 4; i < 0x37; i = i + 1)                    /* clone the serializable body [+4..+0x37) */
+          dg[(unsigned short)(nrec + i)] = dg[(unsigned short)(src + i)];
+        for (f = 0; f < 0xb6; f = f + 1)                    /* first free 0x9fbc registry slot */
+          if (fbc[f * 2] == 0 && fbc[f * 2 + 1] == 0) break;
+        fbc[f * 2] = nrec; fbc[f * 2 + 1] = val;            /* register the new unit -> counted + saved */
+        FUN_1000_66cd(0xd27);                               /* editor status: "TANK ADDED" */
+      }
+    }
+    FUN_0000_d5f9(0,0,0,0x79a9,0,0);                        /* save via the reconstructed serializer */
+    exit(0);
+  }
   if (!(bool)in_CF) {
     FUN_1000_6015();
     DAT_2000_39a8 = 1;
